 "title": "Use advanced vocabulary instead of very",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator suggests replacing common phrases starting with 'very' with single advanced adjectives to sound more elegant and sophisticated. The main lesson is to upgrade basic vocabulary with stronger descriptive words.",
 "key_points": [
  "Instead of 'very important', say 'essential'. Example: 'Getting enough sleep is absolutely essential before a big day.'",
  "Instead of 'very beautiful', say 'magnificent'. Example: 'Look at that view, it's absolutely magnificent.'",
  "Instead of 'very interesting', say 'fascinating'. Example: 'That's a fascinating story, tell me more.'",
  "Instead of 'very good', say 'splendid'. Example: 'You've done a splendid job, well done.'",
  "Instead of 'very surprised', say 'flabbergasted'. Example: 'I was absolutely flabbergasted when I saw the [unclear].'"
 ],
 "content": "Don't say very important, say essential. Getting enough sleep is absolutely essential before a big day. Don't say very beautiful, say magnificent. Look at that view, it's absolutely magnificent. Don't say very interesting, say fascinating. That's a fascinating story, tell me more. Don't say very good, say splendid. You've done a splendid job, well done. Finally, don't say very surprised, say flabbergasted. I was absolutely flabbergasted when I saw the [unclear].",
